From e78960afddd333320bff7e22ce74e5e3109d03c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apranikstar <trialoftheniku@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:28:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] ALFA cards: ARC described by ARCFastSim; cell optics
 and optical tables

The two ALFA cards (Xe 2 bar, C4F10) now use the ray-tracing ARCFastSim module
instead of the calibrated ARCPID formulas (kept as *_ARCPIDformulas.tcl). cards/arc
holds the cell optics tables dumped from the k4geo geometry (ALFA_o1_v01 and the
large-SiPM variant) and the optical tables; examples/ALFA/dump_arc_cells.py makes
the cell table of another geometry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KP5vqAGH2XiGXWtPhaonke
